# Question 03A: RBAC Troubleshooting from Pod Logs

In namespace `audit`, Pod `log-collector` is failing with authorization errors:
`User 'system:serviceaccount:audit:default' cannot list pods in the namespace 'audit'`.

Tasks:
1. Create a ServiceAccount named `log-sa` in namespace `audit`.
2. Create a Role `log-role` in namespace `audit` granting `get`, `list`, and `watch` permissions on `pods`.
3. Create a RoleBinding `log-rb` binding `log-role` to ServiceAccount `log-sa`.
4. Recreate Pod `log-collector` configured with `serviceAccountName: log-sa`.
EOF
cat << 'EOF' > "${LAB_DIR}/q03a-rbac-logs/setup.sh"
#!/bin/bash
set -e
kubectl create ns audit --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
cat << 'EOF' | kubectl apply -f -
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: log-collector
  namespace: audit
spec:
  containers:
  - name: collector
    image: bitnami/kubectl:latest
    command: ["sh", "-c", "while true; do kubectl get pods; sleep 2; done"]
EOF
kubectl delete sa log-sa -n audit --ignore-not-found
kubectl delete role log-role -n audit --ignore-not-found
kubectl delete rolebinding log-rb -n audit --ignore-not-found
echo "Scenario 5 ready. Solve it now!"
EOF
chmod +x "${LAB_DIR}/q03a-rbac-logs/setup.sh"
cat << 'EOF' > "${LAB_DIR}/q03a-rbac-logs/check.sh"
